---
description: Workshop constraints for Cursor agents and Bot-launched cloud runs
alwaysApply: true
---

- Multi-step or Bot-launched work starts with `manager`. Pairing on one seam may pin `builder` mode instead.
- `manager` writes no product code. `builder` is the only implementer.
- Do not write large diffs in the unnamed parent if `manager` or `builder` exists.
- Follow existing patterns. Do not invent a new architecture or framework.
- Improve KITT as voice/driving radio only. Do not rebuild it. Device hands = Bossy (separate). Never brand Sightless/Hermes/Herald/Fleet/Nous as the product name.
- Hermes (`~/.hermes`) is the local brain default. Do not stand up a second one.
- Never commit secrets, tokens, or live Discord / gateway credentials.
- After `builder` finishes, `verifier` before claiming done or opening a PR.
- If the diff touches auth, config, tokens, IPC, HID, or network, spawn `security-auditor` before merge.
- Keep diffs small. One job per PR. No drive-by refactors.
- Use the repo's real check command. Do not invent a test runner.
